From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: Node builds against V8 without
 ArrayBufferView::Buffer()

V8 removed the deprecated `v8::ArrayBufferView::Buffer()` and
`v8::WasmMemoryObject::Buffer()` (V8 233e271021, in Chromium
160.0.8174.0), and `v8::RegExp::Exec` now returns `MaybeLocal<Value>`.
Electron's src_stop_using_deprecated_arraybufferview_buffer.patch only
moved the headers embedders compile, so the engine's Node build failed
in aliased_buffer-inl.h.

- A call that only reads the buffer (Data, GetBackingStore, WasDetached,
  IsDetachable, IsSharedArrayBuffer) uses `GetBuffer()`.
- A call that needs a `Local<ArrayBuffer>` uses
  `GetBuffer().As<v8::ArrayBuffer>()`, which is what `Buffer()` did.
- URLPattern's regex provider keeps `Exec`'s result as a `Value`.

Drop this when Electron's own patches move to a V8 without `Buffer()`.
